 the same as `theseus` and the fork's `pkt/PKT-0058`, and has no uncommitted changes. `git log origin/main..theseus -- word/Drawing/DrawingDocument.js` returns 3d51031, \"Merge pkt/PKT-0078\". So the 27-line difference in that file sits between `origin/main` and the `theseus` base branch, and came from PKT-0078's merge. The scope check seems to compare against `origin/main` instead of the branch this packet was started from (`theseus`), so it blames this packet for PKT-0078's change. It needs fixing in the factory: I can't fix it here without editing `DrawingDocument.js`, which is outside my target. PKT-0085 was probably blocked the same way.\n\n**The diagnosis, unchanged from earlier attempts:**\n- **color-mods:** the test's expected values are wrong, not the code and not the environment. All 257 failures are off by exactly ±1 on one 0–255 channel. sdkjs computes in floating point, while the expected values follow Office's fixed-point truncation.\n- **chartEx-serialize:** a bug in the test page makes it hang the same way every time. The page doesn't load `common/AllFonts.js`, so creating the editor API throws before QUnit starts. Even with that bypassed, the test targets a chartEx XML serializer that this codebase doesn't have.\n- Both suites need edits to sdkjs test files outside the target, so they stay on the oracle's known-broken list. The chartEx wait dropped from 120 s to 20 s, so the oracle run takes about 29 s instead of about 130 s.\n- A request to repair both test pages is already in `.theseus/spawn/`.\n\n**What I did:** recorded the cause of the rejection in the Executor log and added my friction line. `theseus validate` reports 0 errors. Its warning that `sdkjs-common.md` is over the Atlas word limit (876 of 800) was already there before this attempt. Committed as 1521fd9 and 421b411.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- A QUnit page that throws before `QUnit.start()` looks like a timeout. Hooking `QUnit.log` and `pageerror` tells a hang from a slow run.\n-